    "bevel": {
      "word": "BEVEL",
      "definitions": [
        {
          "text": "Any angle other than a right angle; the angle which one surface makes with another when they are not at right angles; the slant or inclination of such surface; as, to give a bevel to the edge of a table or a stone slab; the bevel of a piece of timber.",
          "partOfSpeech": "noun"
        },
        {
          "text": "An instrument consisting of two rules or arms, jointed together at one end, and opening to any angle, for adjusting the surfaces of work to the same or a given inclination; -- called also a bevel square. Gwilt.",
          "partOfSpeech": "noun"
        },
        {
          "text": "Having the slant of a bevel; slanting.",
          "partOfSpeech": "adjective"
        },
        {
          "text": "Hence: Morally distorted; not upright. [Poetic] I may be straight, though they themselves be bevel. Shak. A bevel angle, any angle other than one of 90º. axis. Knight.",
          "partOfSpeech": "adjective"
        },
        {
          "text": "To cut to a bevel angle; to slope the edge or surface of.",
          "partOfSpeech": "verb"
        },
        {
          "text": "To deviate or incline from an angle of 90 Their houses are very ill built, the walls bevel. Swift.",
          "partOfSpeech": "verb"
        }
      ],
